{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120206-infamous","id":120206,"title":"inFamous","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-26T23:30:28-07:00","id":120206,"title":"inFamous","content":"I have always loved this series. Now, with the third installment out and me having played it all the way through, it has inspired me. I would like to run this for my players but not sure what system to use. I have gone through the usual suspects (Aberrant, Hero, GURPS, V&amp;V, Superworld, Silver Age Sentinels and even Brave New World) but the issue I am having is coming up with power packages, so to speak, to allow characters to develop techniques based on a theme. Any suggestions about what to use?<br /> <br /> BTW, for those who have not played the game, let me sum it up. You play someone with electrical powers in the first two. In the third, you get multiple power sets of smoke (A combination of fire and ash and smoke), neon (light based), Video (think a la Green Lantern where you can create things out of pure energy) and concrete (earth based powers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T06:53:27-07:00","id":120314,"title":"","content":"<b>Mutants and Masterminds</b> is still in publication, at least. I'm quite disappointed in the layout of the current edition and think it might possibly be confusing, but have no actual play experience with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T12:22:10-07:00","id":120456,"title":"","content":"I thought about that, too but it lacks the whole package deal thing, tbh. That is what I am going for on this. Now, maybe some tweaking to Aberrant could work with the idea of techniques and such. But not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T19:22:21-07:00","id":120664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120206-infamous?p=120314#post120314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mutants and Masterminds</b> is still in publication, at least. I'm quite disappointed in the layout of the current edition and think it might possibly be confusing, but have no actual play experience with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could really stand to be better. That having been said, the SRD is online and freely accessible and apart from some system terms, is exactly the same. And is a lot more clear.<br /> <br /> It's cleaned up a bit from M&amp;M 2, but is still the same fundamental game, there's still a few powers that can break stuff. but overall it's better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T20:49:20-07:00","id":120707,"title":"","content":"I did enjoy that M&amp;M dispensed with the hit points. It did create a funny situation where the heroes tried to take down a guy whose powers was &quot;I can turn into a large ball and hurl myself at you&quot; but somehow, never rolled less than 18 on his saving throw for like 7 turns. They thought he was indestructible and so I used him later on in future adventures and retconned his origin to make him this super heavyweight.<br /> <br /> But...yeah, I would like to find a gaming system that can accurately reflect, in game mechanics, how to limit the player character to having a set of powers around a theme. Most games leave that up to the GM and the players to self-regulate. I would like to see one have that built-in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T22:01:47-07:00","id":120748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120206-infamous?p=120707#post120707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to find a gaming system that can accurately reflect, in game mechanics, how to limit the player character to having a set of powers around a theme. Most games leave that up to the GM and the players to self-regulate. I would like to see one have that built-in.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Heroes Unlimited</b>, by Palladium. I can't abide the game, because it's class-based without the least bit of balance between classes and built in the days when AD&amp;D ruled the land but game developers thought AD&amp;D's biggest failure was not having enough charts to roll randomized character traits on, but if built-in themes are what you're after, it has them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T06:33:59-07:00","id":120906,"title":"","content":"Ugh. No. Heroes Unlimited is never an option. I can't stand that game. Although, just to punish the minmaxers of my players, I would go ahead and use it to roll up some totally random characters. I did that one time and ended up with an alien that looked like a gorilla with ice powers. <br /> This is the issue I am having. I am trying to get a specific thing accomplished but no game system that I can think of allows it. I am not going to enjoy having to make my own...lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T08:45:35-07:00","id":120957,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'd just make a M&amp;M 3e game with some baseline power options (for things like general durability or being athletic/smart/etc) and have most of the points into a single power with a theme, then have the players add additional powers as alternates on the same power. Just have a game rule that you only get one major power and at least half/three quarters of the points you gain over time have to go into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T12:34:57-07:00","id":121119,"title":"","content":"I may have to do something like that.<br /> For the record though, the DC Heroes system (renamed MEGS) was, in my opinion, the best superhero game system by far. The system was easy to understand. The dice system was easy to figure out. Plus, it allowed for cinematic battles to take place where even a totally human being can take on those who have some small superhuman powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T05:02:37-07:00","id":121633,"title":"","content":"Just to say, I loved the first two infamous games. Haven't played the new one, with the lack of a PS4 and all.<br /> <br /> Anyway, every time I've run anything vaguely superheroish I've used Aberrant(the d10 version).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}